{"shortDescription":"Homebuyers put more down this spring compared to winter, but higher rates pushed monthly payments up 74% over five yearsAUSTIN, Texas, Sept. 24, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Homebuyers put more down this spring than in the winter, but the typical down payment still fell to $27,100, the lowest second quarte…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"i","children":["Homebuyers put more down this spring compared to winter, but higher rates pushed monthly payments up 74% over five years"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["AUSTIN, Texas, Sept. 24, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Homebuyers put more down this spring than in the winter, but the typical down payment still fell to $27,100, the lowest second quarter level since 2021, according to the Realtor.com® second-quarter ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://edge.prnewswire.com/c/link/?t=0\u0026l=en\u0026o=4781271-1\u0026h=2889390162\u0026u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.realtor.com%2Fresearch%2Fdown-payment-report-september-2026\u0026a=Down+Payment+Report","linkText":"Down Payment Report"}},". Down payments fell 9.2% year over year in dollar terms and 0.6 percentage points as a share of purchase price. Increased inventory gave buyers more room to negotiate, while higher mortgage rates kept rate-sensitive households on the sidelines."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"Down payments rose sharply from the winter into spring, as they typically do seasonally, yet the rebound still left them below year-ago levels. Buyers have gained some negotiating room, while higher mortgage rates remain the biggest factor shaping monthly affordability,\" said ",{"type":"b","children":["Hannah Jones, Senior Economist at Realtor.com"]},{"type":"b","children":["®"]},". \"In expensive markets, buyers with more equity are using larger down payments to reduce monthly costs; in softer markets, smaller down payments are adding to the cost of higher rates. For many households, the monthly payment, rather than just the cash needed upfront, will determine how much home they can afford.\""]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Down Payments Rise Seasonally, Remain Below Previous Years"]},"The typical down payment rose to $27,100, or 13.7%, in the second quarter, from $25,000, or 12.9%, in the first quarter of 2026. Although the second quarter is typically the seasonal peak, this year's increase was particularly strong. Still, the median down payment remained below the $29,900 and 14.3% recorded a year earlier."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Primary Residence Down Payments"]}]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Quarter"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Avg. Down Payment as % of Purchase Price"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Median Down Payment ($ amt.)"]}]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["2019 Q2"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["11.2 %"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["$14,000"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["2021 Q2"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["12.6 %"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["$22,300"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["2025 Q2"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["14.3 %"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["$29,900"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["2026 Q2"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["13.7 %"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["$27,100"]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["The rebound continued into the third quarter, with the typical down payment reaching an annual high of $28,800, or 14.0%, in July. That was still 7.5% below year-ago levels in dollar terms and 0.5 percentage points lower as a share of the purchase price."]},{"type":"p","children":["The easing in down payments is consistent with broader housing market conditions. According to",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://edge.prnewswire.com/c/link/?t=0\u0026l=en\u0026o=4781271-1\u0026h=56751137\u0026u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.realtor.com%2Fresearch%2Faugust-2026-data%2F\u0026a=%C2%A0"}}," ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://edge.prnewswire.com/c/link/?t=0\u0026l=en\u0026o=4781271-1\u0026h=2417295437\u0026u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.realtor.com%2Fresearch%2Faugust-2026-data%2F\u0026a=Realtor.com%C2%AE+August+housing+data","linkText":"Realtor.com® August housing data"}},", active listings rose 3.6% year over year, while median list prices fell 1.3%, easing for the 10th consecutive month. Those conditions are giving buyers more time and negotiating room, reducing the pressure to lead with an outsized down payment."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Higher Rates Are Driving the Monthly Payment Burden"]},"Down payments tell only part of the affordability story: the mortgage rate applied to the remaining loan has a larger effect on monthly costs. Even though the typical down payment share was 1.4 percentage points higher than in August 2021, the estimated monthly principal-and-interest payment rose 74% over five years, to $2,376."]},{"type":"p","children":["The comparison below shows how higher mortgage rates drove that increase."]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Measure"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["August 2021"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["August 2025"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["August 2026"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Hypothetical 7% Rate"]}]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Median Listing Price"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["$375,000"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["$429,990"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["$424,500"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["$424,500"]}]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell"