data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["10.5 %"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["-1.6 ppt"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["-1 %"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["58 %"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["$37"]},{"type":"p","children":["more/mo"]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["The contrast is sharp. Higher down payments reduce monthly costs by $205 to $269 in competitive metros, while lower down payments add $37 to $82 per month in softer markets. Austin offers the clearest example. Its typical listing price is down 18% over five years, yet the estimated monthly payment is still up 33% because higher rates have more than offset the price relief and smaller down payments have added to monthly costs."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Northeast Leads on Down Payments as All Regions See Year-Over-Year Declines"]},"The Northeast remained the highest-down-payment region in the second quarter of 2026, with buyers putting down an average 18.1% of the purchase price, followed by the West at 15.2%, the Midwest at 14.2% and the South at 11.9%. All four regions saw year-over-year declines in down payment share."]},{"type":"p","children":["The Northeast also posted the highest median down payment, reflecting higher home prices and persistent competition. Compared with the second quarter of 2019, the region's median down payment was up 238.7%, significantly more than the next-largest increase, 141.0% in the Midwest."]},{"type":"p","children":["The South and West have seen more substantial inventory recovery and softer prices, giving buyers more negotiating room. The regional split is consistent with the Realtor.com Market Clock, which found that 70% of the nation's largest markets either favored buyers or were moving in a buyer-friendly direction in the second quarter of 2026."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"Mortgage rates will remain the biggest swing factor for buyers. If rates continue to rise, down payments and estimated monthly payments are likely to remain elevated as more marginal buyers stay on the sidelines. A sustained decline would do more to improve affordability and bring buyers back into the market, helping keep homeownership within reach for more households,\" Jones said."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Methodology"]},"Down payment trends were analyzed at the national level using Optimal Blue data through August 2026. Down payment as a share of purchase price is calculated as an average across the data. Down payment as a dollar amount is calculated by taking the median across the data. Estimated monthly payments assume a 30-year fixed-rate loan on the average purchase price less the median down payment, amortized at Freddie Mac's Primary Mortgage Market Survey average 30-year fixed rate for the period shown. Comparisons are for Q2, unless otherwise stated; payment comparisons use August data. Estimated payments represent principal and interest only and exclude taxes, insurance, mortgage insurance, HOA fees and other costs of homeownership."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["About Realtor.com"]},{"type":"b","children":["®"]},"For over 30 years, Realtor.com® has connected buyers, sellers, and renters with trusted insights, professional guidance and powerful tools to help them find their perfect home. Recognized as the No. 1 real estate site REALTOR® agents recommend, Realtor.com® delivers consumer connections and a robust suite of marketing tools to support business growth. Realtor.com® is operated by News Corp [Nasdaq: NWS, NWSA] [",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"ASX:NWS","text":"ASX:NWS"}},", NWSLV] subsidiary Move, Inc."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Media Contact: "]},"Janice McDill, ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"http://mailto:press@realtor.com","linkText":"press@realtor.com"}}]},{"type":"p","children":["SOURCE Realtor.com"]}]},"language":"en","tags":[{"title":"Consumer","args":[{"id":"section","value":"consumer"}]},{"title":"Economy","args":[{"id":"category","value":"economic"}]},{"title":"Housing","args":[{"id":"section","value":"housing"}]},{"title":"PR Newswire","args":[{"id":"provider","value":"prnewswire"}]},{"title":"Strategy, business, and products","args":[{"id":"section","value":"strategy_business_products"}]}],"copyright":"Copyright 2026 Cision US Inc. All Rights Reserved.","id":"prnewswire:f91151b56b229:0","title":"Realtor.com®: Down Payments Hit Lowest Q2 Level Since 2021","published":1790244000,"urgency":2,"relatedSymbols":[{"symbol":"ASX:NWS","logoid":"news-corporation","logo":{"style":"single","logoid":"news-corporation"}},{"symbol":"NASDAQ:NWS","logoid":"news-corporation","logo":{"style":"single","logoid":"news-corporation"}}],"storyPath":"/news/prnewswire:f91151b56b229:0-realtor-com-down-payments-hit-lowest-q2-level-since-2021/","read_time":311,"provider":{"id":"prnewswire","name":"PR Newswire","logo_id":"pr_newswire","url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/"}}